        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput_on_all_seven_pollutants",
          "description": "The three worked examples of docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 6.1-6.3, at all seven pollutants where they exist: MY 1980 gasoline, MY 2020 gasoline and MY 2010 diesel, all now on the run's one day type, plus three MY 2020 E85 cells. output_rows is rate-major over the one day types, so an emitting rate row of rank r occupies position r; it occupied 2r-1 (weekend) and 2r (weekday) before the day correction. The H2O aerosol cell is EXACTLY ZERO and its row exists, which is the kind of thing a row count finds and a sum does not. The diesel cells are the ones that carry the sulfate-heavy 2007+ band -- 0.5785 of the composite rather than 0.0665 -- and the 1.086960 PM10 ratio rather than 1.130430.",
